## Writing Principles
- Simple, succinct, technical, factual; lead with the answer
- Active voice, present tense, concrete nouns; `eve` lowercase
- Consistent capability names with architecture overview
- Follow `.agents/skills/technical-writing/` (verify against this repo)
- 300-500 words/section, remove redundancy; no promotional adjectives

## Content Structure
- Title/description → short intro → H2/H3 → examples → related links
- One concept per section; happy path before alternatives
- Personas: intro = evaluate; architecture = mental model; development = task; reference-dense pages = scan

## Navigation
- Max 5-7 top categories, max 2 levels deep; inbound body links, no orphans

## Organization
- DRY: one canonical home; README/homepage summarize and link
- Progressive disclosure; do not invent pages to fill Diátaxis slots
- Semantic feature parity with root README (same capabilities, different copy)

## Layers
- This MDX is canonical **technical** docs. Visual language is root `DESIGN.md`. Rules do not `@`-attach MDX
- READMEs are how to run the app/package; they link here, no duplication
- Update this page when behavior, architecture, commands, or conventions change
